    {
        "chunk_id": "155-5",
        "document_id": "155",
        "policy_title": "Award Nomenclature Policy",
        "heading_level": "h1",
        "section": "Section 5 - Policy Statement",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": null,
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 5,
        "paragraph_end": 7,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=155",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=155",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th October 2024",
        "review_date": "4th October 2027",
        "approval_authority": "Academic Board",
        "approval_date": "4th October 2024",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Section 5 - Policy Statement\n(5)\nLa Trobe University has approved standard nomenclature for all awards granted by the University. All award titles must be aligned with the requirements of the\nAustralian Qualifications Framework\nand the\nAQF Issuance Policy\n. Other minor variations in nomenclature (such as in the use of ‘with’) may be approved by exception where required to meet the requirements of accrediting bodies.\n(6)\nApproved award titles are used in all official certification for those awards, including academic transcripts, testamurs and Australian Higher Education Graduation Statements in accordance with the University’s\nQualifications Issuance Policy\n.\n(7)\nAward titles for courses are approved by Academic Board as part of the course approval process, in accordance with this Policy and the\nCourse and Subject Management Policy\n."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "155-6",
        "document_id": "155",
        "policy_title": "Award Nomenclature Policy",
        "heading_level": "h2",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": "Part A - Broad Nomenclature Requirements for all Awards",
        "topic": null,
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 8,
        "paragraph_end": 8,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=155",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=155",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th October 2024",
        "review_date": "4th October 2027",
        "approval_authority": "Academic Board",
        "approval_date": "4th October 2024",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Part A - Broad Nomenclature Requirements for all Awards\n(8)\nAll award titles will reflect:\nthe level of the award, according to the level or equivalent level in the Australian Qualifications Framework; and\nthe broad field of study, discipline or generic area."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "155-7",
        "document_id": "155",
        "policy_title": "Award Nomenclature Policy",
        "heading_level": "h3",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": "Part A - Broad Nomenclature Requirements for all Awards",
        "topic": "Use of Tags In Award Titles",
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 9,
        "paragraph_end": 9,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=155",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=155",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th October 2024",
        "review_date": "4th October 2027",
        "approval_authority": "Academic Board",
        "approval_date": "4th October 2024",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Use of Tags In Award Titles\n(9)\nFor students who commenced a course from 2022 or who are enrolled in a course version effective from 2022 onwards, the following rules apply to the use of tags in award titles."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "155-8",
        "document_id": "155",
        "policy_title": "Award Nomenclature Policy",
        "heading_level": "h4",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": "Part A - Broad Nomenclature Requirements for all Awards",
        "topic": "Use of Tags In Award Titles",
        "subtopic": "Undergraduate Courses",
        "paragraph_start": 10,
        "paragraph_end": 11,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=155",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=155",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th October 2024",
        "review_date": "4th October 2027",
        "approval_authority": "Academic Board",
        "approval_date": "4th October 2024",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Undergraduate Courses\n(10)\nWhere a student completes a cognate major or majors in an undergraduate course, the award title will include a tag that denotes the cognate major area or areas of study.\n(11)\nWhere an undergraduate course does not offer a cognate major or a student completes an undergraduate course without undertaking a cognate major, the award title will not include a tag."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "155-9",
        "document_id": "155",
        "policy_title": "Award Nomenclature Policy",
        "heading_level": "h4",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": "Part A - Broad Nomenclature Requirements for all Awards",
        "topic": "Use of Tags In Award Titles",
        "subtopic": "Postgraduate Courses",
        "paragraph_start": 12,
        "paragraph_end": 14,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=155",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=155",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th October 2024",
        "review_date": "4th October 2027",
        "approval_authority": "Academic Board",
        "approval_date": "4th October 2024",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Postgraduate Courses\n(12)\nWhere a student completes a cognate specialisation(s) in a postgraduate course, the award title will include a tag that denotes the chosen specialisation(s).\n(13)\nWhere a postgraduate course does not offer a cognate specialisation or a student completes a postgraduate course without a cognate specialisation, the postgraduate award title will not include a tag.\n(14)\nIn all other courses, with the exception of pre-2022 courses that included tags in the award title, the major or specialisation are not included in a tag in the award."
    },
